@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# PR448 module behavior audit
+
+Related issue: [nf-core/atacseq#473](https://github.com/nf-core/atacseq/issues/473). The bounded version and wrapper review is complete. The upstream PR remains gated on the downloadable archive and final review; optional-mode and transitive-dependency limits remain explicit.
+
+The inventory compares the actual merge `a51bee` to its first parent `4177ea`: **267 changed module/subworkflow files**, **70 components**, **16 changed declared dependency versions**, with no unassigned component files. Later history was checked for **36 shared module paths and seven shared subworkflows**. Reviewed current dev is `73155d`. Declared pins and container references are separate; opaque image contents and full transitive dependency sets are not inferred.
+
+| Area                      | Current disposition                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Trim Galore               | Confirmed trimming regression; 2.3.0 plus `--no_poly_g` is validated. [Upstream changelog](https://www.trimgalore.com/reference/changelog/).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
+| Chromap library IDs       | Confirmed regression; shared biological-library IDs restore controlled duplicate marking while preserving distinct read groups.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
+| PRESEQ retry              | Confirmed actual-wrapper option loss: `args.join(' -defects')` empties the String. The local patch preserves original options and appends the flag. Normal success, retry recovery and a failing mutation are checked in Nextflow with a stand-in. Ignoring a failed estimate changed to retrying it; that separate policy change is retained and disclosed.                                                                                                      |
+| Chromap 0.2.4 to 0.3.2    | Upstream includes a best-mapping-pair correction. A local experiment with the real 58/99-base residual pair produces zero alignment records on 0.2.4 and two on 0.3.2. The mapper-stage difference is reproduced independently of trimming/library IDs; attribution to a particular upstream commit is not yet isolated. [Release](https://github.com/haowenz/chromap/releases/tag/v0.3.2).                                                                       |
+| MACS3 3.0.1 to 3.0.4      | Same-input yeast broad/narrow/control checks match. On one full cleaned human BAM with archived broad/BAMPE/no-control arguments, all 30,438 broadPeak rows/fields and non-comment XLS rows match exactly; the 3.0.4 replay matches cloud outputs. `gappedPeak` fields 7-8 become zero, confirmed in the upstream writer and outputs. This does not cover every optional call mode. [Release](https://github.com/macs3-project/MACS/releases/tag/v3.0.4).         |
+| BWA and Bowtie2           | On 5,000 real pairs, BWA alignment fields match; MQ mate tags and the HD header are added. Bowtie2 mapper/index cross-controls have identical alignments, while unique/multiple concordant QC counts change from 2,988/1,556 to 3,039/1,505. These are expected metadata/reporting changes in the tested controls. [BWA](https://github.com/lh3/bwa/releases/tag/v0.7.19), [Bowtie2](https://github.com/BenLangmead/bowtie2/releases/tag/v2.5.4).                 |
+| SAMtools statistics       | Actual 1.19.2 and 1.24 binaries produce identical summary fields on both upstream duplicate/supplementary and zero-insert fixtures, including the known incorrect values. These tested defects predate #448. The later 1.25 tagged source changes those calculations. No new flagstat-normalization, peak or count defect is established. [Fix](https://github.com/samtools/samtools/pull/2388).                                                                  |
+| Picard optical duplicates | Actual 3.1.1 and 3.4.0 both miss one optical duplicate pair when coordinates straddle 32767 at the default 100-pixel distance. Their primary duplicate flags agree. This tested optical-metrics defect predates #448; later 3.5.0 widens physical coordinates. [Fix](https://github.com/broadinstitute/picard/pull/2034).                                                                                                                                         |
+| deepTools matrices        | Actual 3.5.5 and 3.5.6 chromosome-boundary fixtures agree in both matrix modes with `--missingDataAsZero`; this tested behavior is inherited. Later 4.0.0 changes it alongside a major rewrite, so no blind upgrade is proposed. [Release](https://github.com/deeptools/deepTools/releases/tag/4.0.0).                                                                                                                                                            |
+| GFFREAD                   | The optional GFF conversion branch exposes an upstream regression selected by #448. The 0.12.9 packaged tool is the proposed mitigation; historical failure witnesses stay private. Benign conversion is checked using exact pipeline arguments. The HIV GTF inputs cannot cover this path. Genome preparation already decompresses gzip, excluding the separate direct-gzip wrapper trigger. [Release](https://github.com/gpertea/gffread/releases/tag/v0.12.9). |
+| Subread and MultiQC       | Existing debt: overlap precision in retained Subread 2.0.1 and actual local MultiQC 1.13 reporting. The updated nf-core MultiQC entry is unused. Preserve the deliberate fragment-counting/mixed-input pin. [Subread history](https://subread.sourceforge.net/), [MultiQC issue](https://github.com/nf-core/atacseq/issues/463).                                                                                                                                  |
+| Remaining components      | grep/sed, pigz, HTSlib, UCSC and unchanged tool bindings have source/history and wrapper-applicability records. No matching new ordinary-input trigger is established. Absence of a release-note hit is not proof of no defects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
+
+Later wrapper changes were classified as processing, resources, reporting, provenance or packaging. Existing BWA-index and Subread patches must survive module syncs. No subsequent queue/value or library-metadata correction was found in the seven reviewed shared-subworkflow histories.
+
+The full-human MACS control independently verifies the frozen 285,036,036-byte input and archived task arguments. Both versions report 2,569,317 input fragments. Four offline comparison tests pass, and all 47 sealed evidence files rehash without mismatch. An initial harness-only insufficient-temporary-space attempt is retained and excluded; both accepted runs use the same 512 MiB temporary filesystem. Equality covers emitted fields, not hidden numerical precision. No new cloud or Co-Scientist runs were launched.
+
+The GFFREAD mitigation passes the actual-module benign conversion oracle and all nine existing module tests in local `--ci` mode. The isolated suite uses the upstream nft-utils 0.0.9 helper because the pipeline's older 0.0.3 helper lacks the module test's `sanitizeOutput` function. Only version/comment metadata changes in the reviewed snapshots; Conda and SIF execution remain untested.
+
+Detailed inventories, primary-source references and experiments are being assembled in the [reproducibility repository](https://github.com/NicoDeVeaux/atacseq-modules-update-verification). The full-data BWA count match and controlled duplicate-marking recovery meet the two numerical acceptance checks in #473; they do not establish identity across all optional modes.
+
+Source-only scope clarification: BWA and Bowtie2 already assigned technical-run library IDs before #448. This branch restores Chromap's pre-448 behavior; harmonizing the inherited aligner semantics needs separate validation and is not a new finding here.
+
+This is written by GPT-6 (Codex) on Nico DeVeaux's behalf.
